0.323     2026-09-18 02:52:39Z

  - SimpiCI provider: the generated `dzil test` job now exports
    `DZIL_DOCKER_API_SKIP=1`, so a `[@Author::GETTY::Docker]` distribution tests
    on SimpiCI without `dzil test` trying to reach a container engine and build
    an image from inside the CI perl container (its precheck would otherwise
    fail the run). Harmless for a dist without the Docker plugin.
  - SimpiCI provider: a distribution can restrict the Perl matrix with a
    `.simpici-perl` file at its root (whitespace-separated versions, `#`
    comments), overriding the baked-in default. Needed when a dist's
    `.simpici-apt` requires a Debian release the oldest `perl:<ver>` images no
    longer serve packages for. Precedence: `.simpici-perl`, then
    `SIMPICI_PROVIDER_PERL_VERSIONS`, then the default list.

0.322     2026-09-15 20:09:52Z

  - SimpiCI provider: a distribution can now ship a `.simpici-apt` file listing
    apt packages that every generated `dzil test` job installs before building
    its Perl dependencies -- so a dist needing system libraries (e.g. a libgit2-
    backed dist that builds Alien::Libgit2 from source) tests on SimpiCI without
    a hand-written .cicd job. The file is optional; pure-perl dists are unaffected.
  - Add a SimpiCI provider (simpici-provider/): a pinned OCI image that generates
    a `dzil test` job for every supported Perl version, so a distribution can run
    its tests on SimpiCI with only a workflow and no committed .cicd. Published to
    ghcr.io/getty/simpici-dzil-provider and defaulting to Perl 5.22 through 5.44.
  - bundle_config now uses a classic dereference instead of the postfix `->@*`
    form, so the bundle loads on Perl 5.22 (the previous syntax needed 5.24+).

0.321     2026-08-30 05:47:00Z

  - Require Dist::Zilla::Plugin::Docker::API 0.104, which logs the build
    output of a failed image build before aborting, so the [@Author::GETTY::Docker]
    build reports the failing step instead of only the exit status.

0.320     2026-08-19 17:31:57Z

  - LICENSE is now expected as a committed file in the repository.
    Dist::Zilla::Plugin::License is removed from @Basic and
    Dist::Zilla::Plugin::LicenseFile is added in its place, which aborts the
    build when the committed file is missing or no longer matches the dist's
    license, copyright_holder and copyright_year. Hosting platforms only
    detect a licence they can see in the repository, and a generated LICENSE
    never gets there. Write the file with "dzil genlicense" and commit it.
  - New "generate_license" attribute restores the previous behaviour for
    dists that deliberately ship no committed LICENSE.

0.319     2026-08-17 02:38:51Z

  - The commit that records the $VERSION bump after a release now picks up
    executables in "bin/" as well. @Git::VersionManager only allows
    "^lib/.*\.pm$" to be dirty in that commit, while the bump itself rewrites
    ":InstallModules" and ":ExecFiles" — so every distribution with a script
    in "bin/" left the bumped file uncommitted, and git ended up with a "bin/"
    one release behind its "lib/".

0.318     2026-08-08 23:59:18Z

  - "no_cpan" now defaults "version_finder" to ":MainModule", so a
    distribution that never reaches CPAN keeps its $VERSION in the main
    module only. Setting "version_finder" explicitly still wins.

  - Remove the share/claude-skill.yaml ShareDir. It was an outdated copy of
    the Claude skill (last touched in March, still under the old
    "dzil-author-getty" name) that nothing ever read; the skill is
    distributed via .claude/skills instead. This also drops the
    File::ShareDir::Install configure requirement.

0.317     2026-08-04 22:16:54Z

  - Add "tag_format" bundle option, forwarded to Git::Tag.tag_format (or the
    @Git bundle for task/manual_version dists). Defaults to "%v" as before;
    lets a consuming dist.ini override the release tag's format, e.g. to
    "v%v" when a tag also needs to satisfy another ecosystem's tooling (a Go
    module published from the same tag requires strict vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH).

0.316     2026-06-19 14:52:42Z

